From e0666c0cbcb5d7b86d05dc890557aa69378e86d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:53:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] phy: rockchip: inno-dsidphy: pulse the APB reset before
 programming

The driver takes the "apb" reset control in probe and never uses it. Start
from reset defaults after enabling the clocks and runtime power, rather
than
inheriting whatever register state the bootloader left in the PHY. On the
RK3126C tablet this project works on, U-Boot has already driven this same
PHY
in LVDS mode before the kernel touches it.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
index e27fd78b8..25f8dbd08 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-dsidphy.c
@@ -670,6 +670,12 @@ static int inno_dsidphy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	clk_prepare_enable(inno->ref_clk);
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(inno->dev);
 
+	/* Discard the register state the bootloader left behind */
+	reset_control_assert(inno->rst);
+	usleep_range(20, 40);
+	reset_control_deassert(inno->rst);
+	usleep_range(20, 40);
+
 	/* Bandgap power on */
 	phy_update_bits(inno, REGISTER_PART_ANALOG, 0x00,
 			BANDGAP_POWER_MASK, BANDGAP_POWER_ON);
-- 
